							Ok...I got this media lounge thing from dlink. WiFi capable, hooks up to surround sound/tv/etc. You can play streaming music/videos and view pics on your tv with it and all that fun stuff.<br><br>Well, it&#039;s fairly buggy. After about 10 minutes the screen flickers and switches to black and white picture for no reason at all. The remote for it kind of sucks because it is hardly responsive at all.<br><br>There are some other things too. The interface is pretty basic and there aren&#039;t a great deal of options either. The WiFi connection gets slow at time, even when I&#039;m running a 108mbps 802.11g setup (runs fine on laptop). <br><br>To setup a file "server" you install the dlink software on pc/laptop, whatever and select folders you want to share (dlink prog is slow and is gay). Microsoft just came out with their version called media connect which is 100 times better, but eats up so much bandwidth that playing a simple mpeg of an episode of Sealab 2021 without any stalling won&#039;t happen. <br><br>Right now, I&#039;m thinking about packing this bitch back up, returning it to best buy and then looking at the new MS Media Center (reviews are TONS better than this DSM setup.) <br><br>...... wow, long post ......<br><br>Most other options like LinkSys/Netgear/Rokyu/blah blah can&#039;t play videos, and if I can&#039;t stream porn to my 65 in tv, then there&#039;s no point.

